        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.britannica.com/place/Bellevue-Nebraska",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Moses Merrill established Nebraska’s first Christian mission at Bellevue, making it an early missionary center.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bellevue%2C_Nebraska",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1855 Bellevue incorporated and briefly served as the territorial capital before Omaha was chosen.",
